---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const title = 'About';
const description =
  'More than ten years in software across development, testing and QA leadership in India and Australia, and the products and books Priya Kaur builds and writes herself.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      I've worked in software for more than ten years, in India and now in
      Australia. I've been a developer, a test analyst, an automation engineer,
      and a QA lead. I'm based in Brisbane.
    </p>

    <h2>What I've handled</h2>

    <p>
      Across those roles I've owned test strategy and planning, built automation
      frameworks from scratch, run API testing inside CI/CD pipelines, and led
      UAT with business stakeholders. I've been the only QA on projects where
      that meant deciding what "ready to release" actually meant, and standing
      behind it.
    </p>

    <dl class="capabilities">
      <dt class="eyebrow">Testing</dt>
      <dd>
        Test strategy and planning, functional, regression, smoke, UAT,
        exploratory and risk-based testing
      </dd>

      <dt class="eyebrow">Automation</dt>
      <dd>
        Playwright with TypeScript, Page Object Model, Postman API suites in
        CI/CD
      </dd>

      <dt class="eyebrow">Tools</dt>
      <dd>Jira, Azure DevOps, Confluence, Microsoft Dynamics 365</dd>

      <dt class="eyebrow">Building</dt>
      <dd>React Native, Expo, Supabase, TypeScript, Java</dd>
    </dl>

    <p>ISTQB certified.</p>

    <h2>What I build</h2>

    <p>
      Testing taught me what breaks. Building my own products is where I find
      out whether I can avoid it.
    </p>

    <p>
      markAtt is the first — an attendance and homework app for a community
      Sunday school in Brisbane, replacing a Google Sheets workflow. Real users,
      real data, and all the decisions that come with that.
    </p>

    <p>
      I write as well as build. My first children's activity book is on Amazon,
      three more in the series are in progress, and I'm slowly working towards
      something longer.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>

    <p>
      I like understanding why something works, not just that it does. I ask
      questions early rather than guessing, and I'd rather raise a problem while
      it's cheap to fix. Most of the useful work I've done came from talking to
      the people who'd actually use the thing.
    </p>

    <p>
      That curiosity is probably what connects the parts. In testing, the
      interesting bugs are the ones nobody thought to look for. In writing for
      children, you can't hide behind complicated words. Both reward the same
      habit.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      The best way to reach me is email — <a
        href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* A capabilities list: the category in the utility face, the specifics in
     body text. Two aligned columns where there is room, stacked lines where
     there isn't — never a grid of badges. */
  .capabilities {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .capabilities dt {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .capabilities dd + dt {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (min-width: 32rem) {
    .capabilities {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    }

    /* Row gap owns the spacing once the two columns exist. */
    .capabilities dt,
    .capabilities dd + dt {
      margin: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
